%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:dumb -- DumbTcp repairs a loss only after its fixed timeout of 2 s.

The claim (DumbTcp.ned): "a fixed retransmission timeout, no delayed ACKs, no silly window
avoidance and no congestion control"; the timeout is 2 s (DumbTcp.cc).

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms. This test separates DumbTcp: the six algorithms with a fast retransmit repair the loss
within a round trip or two, and TcpNoCongestionControl and TcpVegas, whose RTO is 1 s, repair
it before 2 s.

Host under test: host1, which sends 100000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops
the 15th data segment once. Observation: level 1, the 15th segment goes again only 2 s or
more after its first transmission.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: dumb
%# value: "DumbTcp"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassDumbTcp")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the 15th data segment of host1")
             .within(1.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early 15th data segment again, after the fixed timeout")
              .within(1.95))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("15th data segment again, after the fixed timeout")
             .within(0.65));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassDumbTcp compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "DumbTcp"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassDumbTcp: PASS
